#DESCRIPTION
Reflecting-wall particle-boundary-condition test (pure particle push) - HYBRID PIC
(kinetic ions / massless fluid electrons).

Hybrid counterpart of PARAM.in (full-PIC).  The single kinetic ion species
streams toward the +x wall; both x faces are REFLECTING particle boundaries
(normal velocity flipped, position mirrored).  The shared particle-BC hook
(reflect_or_delete_particle) is exercised in the hybrid cell-centred mover,
so particle number and kinetic energy must be conserved.

The Ohm's law is kept minimal (ideal frozen-in: no Hall, no resistivity, no
electron pressure gradient) so the motional (u x B) field stays small and the
reflecting-wall physics is isolated from hybrid field-evolution artifacts.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
8                       nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
16                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
F                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#FIELDBOXBOUNDARY
conducting              fieldBoxBoundaryLo
conducting              fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi

#PARTICLEBOXBOUNDARY
0                       iSpecies
reflect                 particleBoxBoundaryLo  (x)
reflect                 particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo  (y)
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo  (z)
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi

Standard Maxwell/GMRES solver disabled; use the Ohm's-law + Faraday hybrid
field advance.  The field solver is secondary here -- the particle REFLECT
boundary is the object under test.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

Hall term ON so the Ohm's-law stencil reads the ion moments (rho, momentum) in
the wall ghost cells -- this exercises the hybrid-only centerPlasma ghost BC
(apply_centerPlasma_BC) at the reflecting x-walls.  Resistivity and the
electron-pressure-gradient stay OFF so the motional + Hall fields are the only
drivers.
#HALLTERM
T                       useHallTerm

#BSUBCYCLE
1                       nBSubcycle

#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is the implicit massless
neutralizing fluid.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions
80.0                    ux [km/s]      bulk flow toward +x wall (U_code = 0.8)
4.0                     uy [km/s]      small oblique component (~2.9 deg)
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
0.0                     bx [T]
0.0                     by [T]
5.2195e-9               bz [T]         guide field, tangential to the x-wall
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s]   speed of light cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
100                     npcelx
1                       npcely
1                       npcelz

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 var ascii pic       plotString
-1                      dn
10.0                    dt
1                       dx
rhoS0 uxS0 uyS0 uzS0 Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez   plotVar

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
12.0                    TimeMax   (transit = Lx/U_code = 6.4/0.8 = 8; 12 covers a
                                  full transit + one reflection)

#RUN
